7. Maaseiah the king's son--the sons of Ahaz being too young to take part in a battle, this individual must have been a younger son of the late King Jotham; 

Azrikam the governor of the house--that is, "the palace"; and 

Elkanah that was next to the king--that is, the vizier or prime minister ( Genesis 41:40 Esther 10:3 ). These were all cut down on the field by Zichri, an Israelitish warrior, or as some think, ordered to be put to death after the battle. A vast number of captives also fell into the power of the conquerors; and an equal division of war prisoners being made between the allies, they were sent off under a military escort to the respective capitals of Syria and Israel ( II Chronicles 28:8 ).
